    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "8.13 avg cores of 32 allowed (S5)"
   },
   {
    "code": "no_channel_design",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "no SDRF says which sample is in which channel (no curated design and no deposited SDRF); PXReprise's default design makes each file its own plex and each channel that shows a sample its own sample (marked empty, holding none: 127N in 19 file(s), 127C in 20 file(s), 128N in 18 file(s), 128C in 19 file(s), 129C in 20 file(s), 130N in 20 file(s)); the reporter values compare nothing until a design is curated (QuantProject 079)"
   },
   {
    "code": "no_sdrf",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "No SDRF was found for this dataset, so each channel's sample is the sample its search's TmtDesign.txt names (its `Sample Name`), with nothing else known about it. There is no sample metadata: treat every sample as unannotated."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 1262 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "unresolved_modifications",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "8 modification(s) could not be mapped to a UNIMOD accession or a mass, and are carried in ProForma as [Info:...] tags: UniProt:(3S)-3-hydroxyasparagine on N, UniProt:(3S)-3-hydroxyhistidine on H, UniProt:3'-nitrotyrosine on Y, UniProt:N6-crotonyllysine on K, UniProt:N6-malonyllysine on K, UniProt:N6-succinyllysine on K, UniProt:O-palmitoleoyl serine on S, UniProt:S-(15-deoxy-Delta12,14-prostaglandin J2-9-yl)cysteine on C. Their ptm_sites rows exist and carry modification_name, with modification null, so a query by name finds them and a query by UNIMOD accession will not."
   },
   {
    "code": "isobaric_reference_channels",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "116 channel(s) of the search's TmtDesign.txt are not study samples: `Sample Type` empty: `PXD002528:MS140697-T10:TMT127C`, `PXD002528:MS140697-T10:TMT127N`, `PXD002528:MS140697-T10:TMT128C`, `PXD002528:MS140697-T10:TMT128N`, `PXD002528:MS140697-T10:TMT129C` and 111 more. Their values measure that reference, not a sample of the question. The design is copied in `sources/`."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_ingested",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "PTM site occupancy was not stored: this is a TMT dataset, and MetaMorpheus computes intensity occupancy for label-free searches only; its count occupancy is per file, repeated on every channel (QuantProject DEF-OCC-INT). `ptm_stoichiometry` has no rows here because of that, not because no site was modified."
   }
  ],
